# /design-change

> Generated by `genasis`. The body of this slash command is intentionally
> a thin pointer — the authoritative protocol lives in `GENASIS.md` and
> the per-role overlay fences. The handler agent should read those before
> taking action.

## Behaviour
Run the 5-phase design hot-swap protocol from a reference URL.

## Steps
1. Read `GENASIS.md` § \"Lifecycle\" for the relevant state machine.
2. Identify the issue(s) in scope (argument parsing per command).
3. Take the action with **my** Plane PAT and Mattermost bot — never use
   admin tokens to act on behalf of another role.
4. Post the outcome on the Mattermost issue thread.
5. Run `/record-progress` if the action changed Plane state visible on
   the Kanban board.

## Args
See the command-specific documentation in `docs/COMMANDS.md` once that file
ships in M11. For now, follow the description above.
